user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 12,
    "feature": {
      "name": "quotes_and_refutes_op_factual_claim",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment (OC_comments): explicitly quotes or directly cites a specific factual claim from the OP's title/argument AND refutes that factual claim.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than the OP) jointly. Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly quotes (verbatim or a clear close quotation/block quote) a specific factual claim stated in the OP's title or argument and then disputes/refutes that factual claim (e.g. with counter-evidence or reasoning showing it is false or wrong). Merely mentioning the OP's topic, quoting a value judgment/opinion rather than a factual claim, quoting without refuting, or refuting without quoting gives no credit. The OP argument context is required to verify the quoted text and that it is a factual claim. List order is not chronology; ignore the conversation column. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none qualifies. Return null if OC_comments is missing/unparseable or title and argument are both missing; an empty comment list gives null."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 51,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_quotes_and_refutes_op_phrase",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment (OC_comments): explicitly quotes a specific word/phrase/sentence from the OP's title or argument AND argues against/refutes that quoted text.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument (OP post) and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by other users; order carries no chronology/rank) jointly. Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly quotes (quotation marks, blockquote '>' or clearly verbatim reproduction) a specific phrase or sentence that actually appears in the OP's title or argument, and that same comment disputes, rebuts or argues against the quoted text. Quote of text not in the OP post (e.g., another commenter), quotes only agreed with, or mere topic mentions/paraphrases without verbatim quoting give no qualification. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none qualifies. Return null if OC_comments or the OP text is missing, empty or unparseable. Do not use conversation or any outcome information; note argument may include later edits and no initial snapshot is inferred."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
